        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a1">

                <pb facs="0163" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg43"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Draft of a Proposed Note from Ambassador Shidehara, of
                        the Japanese Delegation, to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the question of the
                    applicability to Japan Proper of the term “insular possessions and insular
                    dominions” used in the Quadruple Treaty signed at Washington on December 13,
                    1921, I have the honor to inquire, under instructions from my Government,
                    whether there is any objection, so far as the United States is concerned, to the
                    conclusion of an agreement supplementary <pb facs="0164" n="44" xml:id="pg44"/>
                    to the said Treaty, to the effect that the term above quoted shall, in its
                    application to Japan, include only Sakhalin, Formosa and the Pescadores, and the
                    islands under the mandate of Japan.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>K. Shidehara</signed></closer>
            </div>
